§§ `Section 2: franchise no-poach [pdf pages 6-7]`

`section 2` MEANS `2: what section 2 says of the agreement`
-- A franchisor and its franchisee: not conditioned on competing for workers (fork F7).
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `businesses that do not compete for workers` `no-hire` `a franchisor and its franchisee` FALSE) EQUALS `scrutiny and per se`
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `businesses whose labor markets are not stated` `no-hire` `a franchisor and its franchisee` FALSE) EQUALS `scrutiny and per se`
-- Among franchisees: the franchisor's sentence needs both its organizing or enforcing and
-- the franchisees' competing for workers (fork F9).
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `competitors for workers` `no-hire` `franchisees of the same franchisor` FALSE) EQUALS `other federal and state laws`
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `businesses that do not compete for workers` `no-hire` `franchisees of the same franchisor` TRUE) EQUALS `other federal and state laws`
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `potentially competing employers` `no-hire` `franchisees of the same franchisor` TRUE) EQUALS `other federal and state laws`
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `businesses whose labor markets are not stated` `no-hire` `franchisees of the same franchisor` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `businesses whose labor markets are not stated` `no-hire` `franchisees of the same franchisor` FALSE) EQUALS `other federal and state laws`
-- Not a no-poach agreement, or no franchise: no sentence of section 2.
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `competitors for workers` `wage fixing at a level` `a franchisor and its franchisee` FALSE) EQUALS JUST EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified agreement` `competitors for workers` `no-hire`) EQUALS JUST EMPTY
-- A no-cold-call clause is a no-poach agreement in substance.
#ASSERT `section 2` (`an identified franchise agreement` `competitors for workers` `not to cold call workers` `a franchisor and its franchisee` FALSE) EQUALS `scrutiny and per se`
#ASSERT `section 2` (`the agreement in full` `the agencies find no agreement between the businesses` `competitors for workers` `no-hire` FALSE `employees` FALSE `a franchisor and its franchisee` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a formal written agreement`) EQUALS JUST EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 2` (`the agreement in full` `whether there is an agreement has not been determined` `competitors for workers` `no-hire` FALSE `employees` FALSE `a franchisor and its franchisee` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a formal written agreement`) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 3: information exchanges [pdf pages 7-8]`

`section 3` MEANS `3: what section 3 says of the exchange`
#ASSERT `section 3` (`a sensitive exchange` `competitors for workers` `directly between the businesses` `the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect`) EQUALS JUST (LIST `may violate`, `effect found`, `may indicate`)
-- The contrary finding: the effect sentence is not given, and nothing is said in its place
-- (fork F12).
#ASSERT `section 3` (`a sensitive exchange` `competitors for workers` `directly between the businesses` `the exchange neither has nor is likely to have an anticompetitive effect`) EQUALS JUST (LIST `may violate`, `may indicate`)
-- Intent, explicitness, adherence, discretion and the transaction are not read.
#ASSERT `section 3` (`the exchange in full` `competitors for workers` TRUE `directly between the businesses` FALSE `the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST (LIST `may violate`, `effect found`, `may indicate`)
#ASSERT `section 3` (`the exchange in full` `competitors for workers` FALSE `through an algorithm or other software, or through a third party's tool or product` TRUE `the exchange's effect has not been assessed` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (LIST `recommendations`)
#ASSERT `section 3` (`the exchange in full` `competitors for workers` FALSE `directly between the businesses` TRUE `the exchange's effect has not been assessed` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (LIST `an agreement to use shared wage recommendations, lists, calculations, or algorithms can also still be unlawful even where co-conspirators retain some discretion or cheat on the agreement`)
#ASSERT `section 3` (`the exchange in full` `competitors for workers` FALSE `directly between the businesses` TRUE `the exchange's effect has not been assessed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (LIST `even if the companies are parties to a legitimate transaction or a joint venture or other collaborative activity, an agreement between them to share information about wages or other terms of employment may violate the antitrust laws`)
-- Recommendations from a direct exchange: not the third-party sentence.
#ASSERT `section 3` (`the exchange in full` `competitors for workers` TRUE `directly between the businesses` TRUE `the exchange's effect has not been assessed` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (LIST `may violate`, `effect pending`, `may indicate`)
-- Through an intermediary and through an algorithm or tool read alike (fork F25).
#ASSERT `section 3` (`a sensitive exchange` `competitors for workers` `through an algorithm or other software, or through a third party's tool or product` `the exchange's effect has not been assessed`) EQUALS `section 3` (`a sensitive exchange` `competitors for workers` `through a third party or intermediary` `the exchange's effect has not been assessed`)
-- Information that is not competitively sensitive, shared directly, with nothing else found.
#ASSERT `section 3` (`the exchange in full` `competitors for workers` FALSE `directly between the businesses` TRUE `the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST EMPTY
-- Only with competitors: potential competitors and non-competitors get nothing; the guard
-- when it is not stated (fork F13).
#ASSERT `section 3` (`a sensitive exchange` `potentially competing employers` `directly between the businesses` `the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect`) EQUALS JUST EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 3` (`a sensitive exchange` `businesses that do not compete for workers` `directly between the businesses` `the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect`) EQUALS JUST EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 3` (`a sensitive exchange` `businesses whose labor markets are not stated` `directly between the businesses` `the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect`) EQUALS NOTHING

