§§ `Section 5: other restrictive conditions [pdf pages 10-11]`

`section 5` MEANS `5: what section 5 says of the term`
`depending: training repayment` MEANS `depending on the facts and circumstances, a training repayment agreement provision can be anticompetitive`
`depending: non-solicitation` MEANS `depending on the facts and circumstances, a non-solicitation agreement that prohibits a worker from soliciting former clients or customers of the employer can be anticompetitive`
`depending: exit fee` MEANS `depending on the facts and circumstances, an exit fee or liquidated damages provision can be anticompetitive`
-- A non-disclosure agreement of such scope that it prevents leaving: "when" is a condition
-- (fork F16).
#ASSERT `section 5` (`a term that prevents leaving` `a non-disclosure agreement`) EQUALS LIST `non-disclosure agreements can violate the antitrust laws when they span such a large scope of information that they function to prevent workers from seeking or accepting other work or starting a business after they leave their job`, `same concerns`, `state limits`
#ASSERT `section 5` (`a bare term` `a non-disclosure agreement`) EQUALS LIST `same concerns`, `state limits`
#ASSERT `section 5` (`the term in full` `a non-disclosure agreement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `may also investigate`, `same concerns`, `state limits`
-- "Depending on the facts and circumstances": without the text's example finding, the
-- hedged sentence alone (fork F16).
#ASSERT `section 5` (`a bare term` `a training repayment agreement provision`) EQUALS LIST `depending: training repayment`, `same concerns`, `state limits`
#ASSERT `section 5` (`a bare term` `a non-solicitation agreement that prohibits the worker from soliciting former clients or customers of the employer`) EQUALS LIST `depending: non-solicitation`, `same concerns`
#ASSERT `section 5` (`a bare term` `an exit fee or liquidated damages provision`) EQUALS LIST `depending: exit fee`, `same concerns`
#ASSERT `section 5` (`the term in full` `a training repayment agreement provision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `depending: training repayment`, `same concerns`, `the agencies may investigate if there are indications that such a restrictive condition on workers is harming competition`, `state limits`
-- The unnamed kind: only the first sentence, and only on its finding (fork F17).
#ASSERT `section 5` (`a bare term` `another restrictive, exclusionary, or predatory employment condition`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 5` (`the term in full` `another restrictive, exclusionary, or predatory employment condition` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `may also investigate`
#ASSERT `section 5` (`the term in full` `another restrictive, exclusionary, or predatory employment condition` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- A non-compete clause is section 4's (fork F18); section 4's findings are not read here.
#ASSERT `section 5` (`the term in full` `a non-compete clause` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 5` (`the term in full` `a non-disclosure agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `same concerns`, `state limits`

